{title: Sing Till The Power}
{key: Bb}
{x_theme: praise, faith-trust, victory}
{x_source: chrd:sing_till_the_power.chrd}

{comment: Verse 1}
[Bb]Without a sound God's children marched
A[Eb]round Jericho six [Bb]days
But on the seventh morn', Joshua said "Blow your [Gm]horn
And [C7]lift your voice in [F]praise
And as a [Bb]song of triumph began to ring
On the [Eb]seventh time a[C7/E]round
Well the [Eb]rocks started [C7/E]crumblin'
And the [Bb/F]walls started [G7]tumblin'
As the [Cm]power of the [F]Lord came [Bb]down

{comment: Chorus}
[Bb]Sing 'till the power of the Lord comes down
Sing 'till the power of the [C]Lord comes [F]down
Lift up your head; don't be afraid
[Gm]Lift up your head; [G7]don't be afraid
[Cm]Sing '[Bb/D]till the [Cm/Eb]power of the [Bb/F]Lord     [F7]comes [Bb]down

{comment: Verse 2}
[Bb]Paul and Silas in a Roman jail
[Eb]Seemed all hope was [Bb]gone
But though their hands were tied, and their feet [Gm]bound
Still [C7]they had a song[F]
So at the [Bb]midnight hour, when they began to sing
They hea[Eb]rd a rumblin' [C7/E]sound
The earth [Eb]started sha[C7/E]kin'
And their chains started breakin'
As the [Cm]power of the [F]Lord came [Bb]down

{comment: Verse 3}
[Bb]Now when you've found yourself in a valley low
[Eb]And it seems you [Bb]can't go through
Well the same God that rocked the jail long ago
Can do the same for [Gm]you
So lift your [Bb]voice and let a song of faith ring out
And watch the walls come tumblin' down
[Eb]Yes, it's ama[C7/E]zin'
[Eb]When we start [C7/E]praisin'
The [Cm]power of the [F]Lord comes [Bb]down
